# 3-qubit Quantum Fourier Transform, written in the elementary gate set.
# Each controlled-phase CP(theta) is decomposed into two rz's and two cx's:
#   CP(theta) = rz(theta/2)_c rz(theta/2)_t cx rz(-theta/2)_t cx
# test_examples.py proves this circuit's unitary equals the 8-point DFT matrix
# up to global phase. q0 is the least-significant qubit; the final swap performs
# the QFT's bit-reversal.
qubits 3
# H on the top qubit, then phase-rotate it by the lower qubits.
h q2
rz(pi/4) q1
rz(pi/4) q2
cx q1, q2
rz(-pi/4) q2
cx q1, q2
rz(pi/8) q0
rz(pi/8) q2
cx q0, q2
rz(-pi/8) q2
cx q0, q2
# H on the middle qubit, phase-rotated by the bottom qubit.
h q1
rz(pi/4) q0
rz(pi/4) q1
cx q0, q1
rz(-pi/4) q1
cx q0, q1
# H on the bottom qubit; then reverse the bit order.
h q0
swap q0, q2
